        "text": "A small home helps with this particular grief in a few ways. With a handful of residents instead of dozens, caregivers learn her stories quickly: the street she grew up on, the garden she kept, the dog's name. So when she asks about the house, someone who knows her can sit down and talk about the roses instead of reciting a script. She can bring her own things to make her space feel like hers. And because it is a home, with a kitchen, the smell of dinner, and a back door, it is closer to what she is actually missing. We work with families using Medicaid COPES as well as private pay, and we are glad to talk through how the pieces fit, but we are not lawyers, and we will tell you plainly when a question belongs to an attorney."
